{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Therefore it is said, etc.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory derived two interpretations from the verse: First (Kiddushin 30b), that the verse speaks of the war of Torah, which is the war of HaShem — for although they become haters of one another in halakhah, in the end they become lovers; this is the meaning of <b>et vahev besufah</b>. Second (Berakhot 54a), that two men afflicted with tzara'at were in Israel, one named Et and one named Vahev, and they would walk at the edge of the camp because they were metzora'im, and they would publicize the miracle — how the mountains would clash together, etc. — up to here." "<b>Now it appears</b> to explain the verse by way of peshat: since He mentioned the Arnon as the border of Moab and said of it <b>for Arnon is the border of Moab</b> — meaning, and Israel have no portion in it — therefore He concluded <b>therefore it is said in the book</b>, meaning, in the book that is before HaShem, concerning the wars that He allocates to the nations — taking from this one and giving to that one. And there too it is said, that HaShem will give Israel an inheritance from the nations, as He promised to the Fathers. And He said <b>it is said</b>, for there in the book it will be said concerning this border that they will give it to Israel besufah, and not at that time, but with the coming of our Mashiach — then HaShem will give us Moab and its border as an inheritance, for it is one of the three that remain for us to inherit: the Kenite, the Kenezite, and the Kadmonite (Genesis 15:19)." "And the meaning of the word <b>vahev</b> is explained in two ways: the first, the language of love — on this reading, that HaShem loved to give it at the end and not now; or, the language of giving, after the manner of (Daniel 2:21) ״יָהֵב חָכְמְתָא לְחַכִּימִין״. And we find that Scripture sometimes uses a word in Aramaic translation, as in (Genesis 21:7) ״מִי מִלֵּל לְאַבְרָהָם״, and ״וְאָתָה מֵרִבְבוֹת קֹדֶשׁ״ (Deuteronomy 33:2)." "And His saying <b>and the streams, etc.</b> — meaning, He comes to delineate the border of Moab that is written in the Book of the Wars of HaShem, which HaShem is destined to give us. And He said ״and the streams״ of Arnon are also included in what is given to Israel — also the slope of the streams that stretches, etc."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:11:54.533928565Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}